.TH "RTCPEERCONNECTIONICEERROREVENT.ERRORTEXT" "3JS" "May 15, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent.errorText \-
RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent: errorText property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]errorText\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent\f[R] interface represents the STUN
error reason text returned by the STUN or TURN server if there was an
error during ICE negotiation.
.PP
If communication with the STUN or TURN server couldn\(cqt be established
at all, this will be a browser\-specific string explaining the error.
.SH VALUE
A string returned by the STUN or TURN server, or a browser\-specific
string explaining why communication with the server could not be
established.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example creates a handler for \f[CR]icecandidateerror\f[R] events,
which creates human\-readable messages describing the local network
interface for the connection and the ICE server used to attempt the
connection.
It then calls a function to display those messages and the value of the
event\(cqs \f[CR]errorText\f[R] property.
.IP
.EX
pc.addEventListener(\(dqicecandidateerror\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] networkInfo = \(ga[Local interface: ${event.address}:${event.port}]\(ga;
  \f[B]const\f[R] iceServerInfo = \(ga[ICE server: ${event.url}]\(ga;

  showMessage(event.errorText, iceServerInfo, networkInfo);
});
.EE
